  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Old Ancestor Xue Hu questions him over soft jade sand that has not been fully collected. Despite a fierce reputation and rebellious nature, Li Peng Wang lowers his head and reports that a sky chief beast group forced him to stop, and that he will succeed if he returns to white heaven. Xue Hu warns that this first round failure already threatens his place as fourth peak owner. Lady Wan Shou later says he was heavily injured yet still brought back a portion of soft jade sand. Xue Hu ties that bad luck to Fortune Rivalling Heaven’s backlash against acts that would harm Ma Hong Yun.",
      "chapters": [
        772
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_old_ancestor_xue_hu",
        "char_lady_wan_shou",
        "gu_fortune_rivalling_heaven_immortal_gu",
        "char_ma_hong_yun"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "He is tall with a fierce aura, long eyebrows, an aquiline nose, and eyes shining with a sharp light. His ears are not human ears. They look like wings and shine in golden light.",
      "chapters": [
        812
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "He leads Demon Lord Long Dan and Gong Zi Mo as three demonic path Gu Immortals into the site where Dong Fang Chang Fan was killed, still named as owner of Snowy Mountain’s fourth peak.",
      "chapters": [
        812
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
